  "body": "Conjecture: recover_json_object gives the same answer on two replies that its documented rule requires it to tell apart. The rule I am reading is: \"The object scored is the last one inside a code fence when any fence holds one, else the last top-level object in the text\". Reply A is:\n```json\n{\"a\":1}\n```\n```json\n{\"b\":2} {\"c\":3}\n```\nReply B is:\n```json\n{\"a\":1}\n```\nFor Reply A, the rule requires the last object inside a code fence, which is {\"c\":3}. For Reply B, the rule requires {\"a\":1}. The function returns {\"a\":1} for both, so the difference is lost. What would make me wrong: if recover_json_object(Reply A) returns {\"c\":3} (or any object other than {\"a\":1}), or if recover_json_object(Reply B) returns something other than {\"a\":1}, then the pair is not a same-answer pair and the conjecture is false.",
